{"format":1,"key":"zone:westfall","path":"/lore/zone/westfall","name":"Westfall","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"westfall","name":"Westfall","path":"/lore/zone/westfall"},"levels":"Levels 10-20","description":"Westfall's farms lie exposed, and the Defias Brotherhood holds much of the countryside. Once Stormwind's breadbasket, the territory now struggles without…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:westfall","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Westfall's farms lie exposed, and the Defias Brotherhood holds much of the countryside. Once Stormwind's breadbasket, the territory now struggles without crown support or military garrisons.","Westfall once fed the Kingdom of Stormwind with its pastures and wheat fields. After the Second War, the kingdom's finances ran thin and its leaders neglected the territory. Stormwind sent resources elsewhere and let its garrisons go, leaving the land fallow. Now barren pastures, harsh coastal winds, rogue harvest golems, and Riverpaw gnolls make survival hard for the few homesteaders who remain.","The Defias Brotherhood's arrival hastened Westfall's collapse. The bandits wear red masks and follow a leader whose name no one in the countryside knows. They made Westfall their stronghold, burning farmers' fields, salting the soil, and taking abandoned mines. From Moonbrook, a ghost town, the Brotherhood rules most of the countryside in all but name.","The House of Nobles has ignored Westfall's plight, so local people have taken up their own defense. At Sentinel Hill, Gryan Stoutmantle formed the People's Militia, a volunteer force holding the line against gnolls and bandits. Stormwind sends no formal soldiers or supplies. The Militia depends on wandering adventurers to push back the Defias and protect the farms that remain."],"hash":"8dd71d","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"7a41a6da2c","sec":80},"female-narrator":{"sha":"180d5bbf7d","sec":83}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Westfall (Classic)","u